{"name":"Light Rattan","hex":"#d1c1aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"rattan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several species of climbing palm of the genus Calamus.","The plant used as a material for making furniture, baskets etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To beat with a rattan cane."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rattan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rattan","blocks":[{"text":"Rattan, also spelled ratan, is the name for roughly 600 species of Old World climbing palms belonging to subfamily Calamoideae. The greatest diversity of rattan palm species and genera are in the closed-canopy old-growth tropical forests of Southeast Asia, though they can also be found in other parts of tropical Asia and Africa. Most rattan palms are ecologically considered lianas due to their climbing habits, unlike other palm species. A few species also have tree-like or shrub-like habits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Thatiyan_Cuural_%28Malayalam-_%E0%B4%A4%E0%B4%9F%E0%B4%BF%E0%B4%AF%E0%B4%A8%E0%B5%8D%E2%80%8D_%E0%B4%9A%E0%B5%82%E0%B4%B0%E0%B4%B2%E0%B5%8D%E2%80%8D%29_%285661614812%29.jpg/330px-Thatiyan_Cuural_%28Malayalam-_%E0%B4%A4%E0%B4%9F%E0%B4%BF%E0%B4%AF%E0%B4%A8%E0%B5%8D%E2%80%8D_%E0%B4%9A%E0%B5%82%E0%B4%B0%E0%B4%B2%E0%B5%8D%E2%80%8D%29_%285661614812%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rattan","wikidata":"Q323021"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Daemonorops_mollis_%28rattan_palm%29_-_Bukidnon_Philippines.jpg/500px-Daemonorops_mollis_%28rattan_palm%29_-_Bukidnon_Philippines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Daemonorops_mollis_%28rattan_palm%29_-_Bukidnon_Philippines.jpg/1280px-Daemonorops_mollis_%28rattan_palm%29_-_Bukidnon_Philippines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Daemonorops_mollis_%28rattan_palm%29_-_Bukidnon_Philippines.jpg/500px-Daemonorops_mollis_%28rattan_palm%29_-_Bukidnon_Philippines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Juvenile Calamus oblongus subsp. mollis in a forest understory in the Philippines","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaemonorops_mollis_(rattan_palm)_-_Bukidnon_Philippines.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Rattan_Palm_%28Calamus_rotang%29_with_fruits_%287844049166%29.jpg/500px-Rattan_Palm_%28Calamus_rotang%29_with_fruits_%287844049166%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia